-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the dates and choices used below`

`1 Jan 1990` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 1990
`31 Jan 1998` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 1 1998
`1 Feb 1998` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 2 1998
`29 Feb 2004` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2004
`15 Jun 2000` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 6 2000
`10 Mar 2019` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 3 2019
`29 Feb 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2020
`16 Jun 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 16 6 2025
`2 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 3 2026
`9 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 9 3 2026
`10 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 3 2026
`11 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 11 3 2026
`15 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2026
`16 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 16 3 2026
`17 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 17 3 2026
`20 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 20 3 2026
`23 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 23 3 2026
`24 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 24 3 2026
`25 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 25 3 2026
`28 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 3 2026
`30 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 3 2026
`31 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 3 2026
`1 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 4 2026
`2 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 4 2026
`4 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 4 4 2026
`5 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 5 4 2026
`9 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 9 4 2026
`12 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 12 4 2026
`15 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 4 2026
`19 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 19 4 2026
`20 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 20 4 2026
`30 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 4 2026
`2 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 3 2027
`2 Mar 2029` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 3 2029

`ADULT` MEANS `an adult who is not a legally incompetent person`
`INCOMPETENT` MEANS `a legally incompetent person`
`CHILD` MEANS `a child (under 12)`
`MATURE YP` MEANS `a young person with sufficient maturity and developmental capacity to understand the request and the record`
`IMMATURE YP` MEANS `a young person without that maturity and capacity`
`DEAD WITH REP` MEANS `dead, and there is a legal representative`
`DEAD NO REP` MEANS `dead, and there is no legal representative`

`HSP RECORD` MEANS `a record held by a health service provider`
`OTHER WITH PHI` MEANS `a record held by someone else that contains personal health information about me`
`OTHER NO PHI` MEANS `a record held by someone else that contains no personal health information about me`
`FACTUAL` MEANS `factual matters (history, examination findings, test results, diagnosis, treatment plan, action taken)`
`OPINION` MEANS `matters of opinion`
`NOT CONFIDENTIAL` MEANS `nothing in this part was given in confidence`
`BY ME` MEANS `me, my guardian or a person with parental responsibility for me`
`BY TREATING HSP` MEANS `a health service provider in the course of, or in relation to, treating me`
`BY SOMEONE ELSE` MEANS `someone else (not me, my guardian, a parent or a treating provider)`

`ACCESS YES` MEANS `yes: you have a right of access to this part (s 10 (1)), and none of ss 10 (2), 14, 14A, 15 or 17 stands in the way`
`ACCESS OUT` MEANS `NOTHING-kind: s 10 (1) gives no right of access to a record held by someone other than a health service provider that contains no personal health information about you`
`OLD OPINION` MEANS `no (the text's no): this part is matter of opinion recorded before 1 February 1998 (s 10 (1) (d)); factual matters in it can still be seen`
`LAW BARS` MEANS `no: access would contravene a territory or Commonwealth law or a court order (s 10 (2) (a), s 14 (c))`
`NOT HELD` MEANS `the record keeper may refuse: it does not have possession, custody or control of this part (s 14 (a))`
`NOT MINE` MEANS `the record keeper may refuse: this part does not relate to you in any respect (s 14 (b))`
`S14A BARS` MEANS `no: the record keeper must not give access -- it relates to a child protection report and identifies the reporter (s 14A)`
`S15 BARS` MEANS `no: the record keeper must not give access -- it believes on reasonable grounds that the information would be a significant risk to life or health (s 15); see ss 16-16D if the risk is to you`
`S17 BARS` MEANS `no: the record keeper must not give access -- this part is subject to confidentiality (s 17)`

`INSPECT` MEANS `inspect the record (or a print-out of an electronic record) and take notes`
`COPY` MEANS `receive a copy of the record`
`EXPLAIN` MEANS `view the record and have it explained`

`ME ASKING` MEANS `I am the consumer, asking personally`
`PARENT ASKING` MEANS `a person with parental responsibility for a child or young person`
`GUARDIAN ASKING` MEANS `a guardian of a legally incompetent person`
`REP ASKING` MEANS `a legal representative of a deceased consumer`
`FAMILY ASKING` MEANS `an immediate family member of a deceased consumer with no legal representative`
`WRITING NEEDED` MEANS `yes: this request must be in writing (s 12 (2) (d))`
`ORAL OK` MEANS `no, it may be oral; but the record keeper may ask for it in writing and need do nothing more on the oral request until then (s 12 (3))`
`REQUEST OK` MEANS `yes: the request is properly made, and the record keeper must answer within 2 weeks after receiving it (s 13 (2))`
`REQUEST INCOMPLETE` MEANS `no: the request does not have everything s 12 (2) requires (name, address unless known, the record identified, the way of access, writing where required)`
`ORAL PUT IN WRITING` MEANS `no: it was oral and the record keeper asked you to make it in writing, so nothing more need be done on the oral request (s 12 (3), s 13 (1) (b))`

`NO FEE DAY` MEANS `no deadline yet: the fee stated in the notice has not been paid`
`NO DUTY` MEANS `no duty on these facts (the text's no)`

`NO ANSWER` MEANS `no answer yet`
`ACCESS ANSWER` MEANS `access given, or a notice that access will be given on payment of a stated fee`
`REFUSAL NOTICE` MEANS `a notice refusing access to the whole record on a s 14 ground, or saying s 14A, 15 or 17 forbids access`
`REFERRAL NOTICE` MEANS `a notice that the health services commissioner has referred the request to the provider who prepared the record`
`TAKEN REFUSED NO ANSWER` MEANS `yes: no answer within 2 weeks after the request was received (s 13 (2); s 13D (a) (i)); you may complain (s 18 (1) (b), (c))`
`TAKEN REFUSED LATE ACCESS` MEANS `yes: access was not given by the day s 13B (2) or s 13BA (2) sets (s 13D (a) (iii)); you may complain (s 18 (1) (b), (c))`
`TAKEN REFUSED ARRANGEMENTS` MEANS `yes: the arrangements to inspect the record or have it explained were unreasonable (s 13D (b)-(d)); you may complain (s 18 (1) (b), (c))`
`REFUSED BY NOTICE` MEANS `refused, not just taken to be: the record keeper refused by notice (s 13 (2) (b), (c)); you may complain (s 18 (1) (b), (c))`
`NOT REFUSED EVIDENCE` MEANS `not refused: the record keeper need not give access, because the evidence of identity or authority it asked for was not given or did not satisfy it (s 13B (4), s 13BA (6))`
`NOT REFUSED REFERRED` MEANS `not refused: the request was referred to the provider who prepared the record, which is taken to have received it under s 12 (s 10 (6)); ask again about that provider`
`NOT REFUSED IN TIME` MEANS `not refused: access was given in time`
`NOT YET` MEANS `not yet: the time has not run out`
`NOT YET FEE` MEANS `not yet: you have been told of a fee, and no day for access runs until it is paid`

`SIGNED ME` MEANS `signed by the consumer personally`
`SIGNED PARENT` MEANS `signed by a person with parental responsibility for the consumer`
`SIGNED GUARDIAN` MEANS `signed by a guardian of the consumer`
`SIGNED REP` MEANS `signed by the legal representative of the deceased consumer`
`SIGNED OTHER` MEANS `signed by someone else`

`NO OFFER` MEANS `no offer to discuss the record was made`
`OFFER DECLINED` MEANS `an offer was made and I did not accept it`
`DISCUSSED UNSATISFIED` MEANS `I discussed the record with the provider named in the offer and am not satisfied`
`DISCUSSED SATISFIED` MEANS `I discussed the record with the provider named in the offer and am satisfied`
`SAME BOARD` MEANS `is registered with the same national board as the provider who wrote the record`
`MEDICAL` MEANS `is a registered medical practitioner able to understand and interpret the record`
`SAME KIND` MEANS `provides the same kind of service as the provider who wrote the record, and is able to understand and interpret it`
`NONE OF THESE` MEANS `none of these`
`NOMINEE YES` MEANS `yes: the record (or a copy) must be given to your nominee within 2 weeks after the nomination was received (s 16B (2))`
`NOMINEE OBJECTED` MEANS `no (the text's no): the record keeper objected to your nominee within the 2 weeks, as s 16D allows (s 16B (3) (a)); you may nominate another`
`NOMINEE LAPSED` MEANS `no (the text's no): the nomination lapsed, because the record keeper gave you access under s 16B, or your nominee died, stopped practising, refused or did not act in reasonable time (s 16A (3), s 16B (3) (b)); you may nominate another`
`NOMINEE OBJECTION VOID` MEANS `yes: the record keeper's objection does not count, because s 16D (4) forbids objecting to this nominee or it was given out of time; the record must be given within 2 weeks (s 16B (2))`

`ASKED OTHER` MEANS `someone asked a person other than me for a health status report about me`
`GAVE OTHER` MEANS `someone gave a health status report about me to a person other than me`
`OBTAINED` MEANS `someone obtained a health status report about me from a health service provider`
`NOT HSR` MEANS `s 7 does not apply: this is not a health status report (the text's no)`
`HSR UNDER LAW` MEANS `s 7 does not apply: it is done in accordance with a territory or Commonwealth law or a court order (s 7 (5))`
`HSR NO` MEANS `no (the text's no): not without your consent, and you have not given a valid one (s 7 (1), (2), (4))`
`HSR YES` MEANS `yes, with your consent: and they must tell you in writing that you may ask for a copy and give them comments, give you a copy as soon as practicable if you ask, and consider and keep your comments with the report (s 7 (3))`

`KEEP IT` MEANS `no (the text's no): the record keeper must keep it and must not destroy it, even if it is inaccurate (principle 4.1 cl 2)`
`DESTROY LAW` MEANS `yes: a territory law requires or allows its destruction (principle 4.1 cl 3 (a))`
`DESTROY TIME` MEANS `yes: the age or time in principle 4.1 cl 3 (b) has passed and no other law prohibits destruction (it must then go on the register of destroyed records, principle 4.2)`
`DESTROY COPY` MEANS `yes: an accessible electronic copy has been made as the Electronic Transactions Act 2001 s 11 (2) (b) describes (principle 4.1 cl 3 (c))`
`DESTROY FOOTAGE` MEANS `yes: it is surveillance footage from a security camera at or around the premises (principle 4.1 cl 3 (d))`

`SENT IN TIME` MEANS `sent in time`
`NOT SENT STILL IN TIME` MEANS `not yet sent, still in time`
`SENT LATE` MEANS `late: not sent by the day principle 12.1 or 12.2 sets (a breach of the privacy principles you may complain about, s 18 (1) (a))`
`SENT NO DAY` MEANS `no day is set yet: the fee has not been paid`

§ `Who can ask for access (ss 10 (8), 10A, 25-27)`

#ASSERT `ss 10A, 25-27 -- who can ask for access` `ADULT` EQUALS `the consumer personally`
#ASSERT `ss 10A, 25-27 -- who can ask for access` `INCOMPETENT` EQUALS `a guardian of the consumer`
#ASSERT `ss 10A, 25-27 -- who can ask for access` `CHILD` EQUALS `the person with parental responsibility for the consumer`
-- Finding 1: s 10A (b) (i) prevails over s 25 (b) for the mature young person.
#ASSERT `ss 10A, 25-27 -- who can ask for access` `MATURE YP` EQUALS `the consumer personally`
#ASSERT `ss 10A, 25-27 -- who can ask for access` `IMMATURE YP` EQUALS `the person with parental responsibility for the consumer`
#ASSERT `ss 10A, 25-27 -- who can ask for access` `DEAD WITH REP` EQUALS `the legal representative of the deceased consumer`
#ASSERT `ss 10A, 25-27 -- who can ask for access` `DEAD NO REP` EQUALS `an immediate family member of the deceased consumer`

§ `The right of access (ss 10, 14, 14A, 15, 17)`

-- A hospital record, factual, 1990, nothing standing in the way: factual matters whenever recorded.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `1 Jan 1990` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ACCESS YES`
-- An opinion recorded the day before commencement, and on the day of commencement.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `OPINION` `31 Jan 1998` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OLD OPINION`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `OPINION` `1 Feb 1998` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ACCESS YES`
-- A factual part from 1990 is not caught by s 10 (1) (d).
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `31 Jan 1998` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ACCESS YES`
-- An insurer's file with my health information; and one with none.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `OTHER WITH PHI` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ACCESS YES`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `OTHER NO PHI` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ACCESS OUT`
-- Each bar on its own.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `LAW BARS`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT HELD`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT MINE`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S14A BARS`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S15 BARS`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `BY SOMEONE ELSE` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S17 BARS`
-- Material given in confidence by me, or by a treating provider, is not "subject to confidentiality" (s 17 (2) (a)-(d)).
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `BY ME` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ACCESS YES`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `BY TREATING HSP` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ACCESS YES`
-- s 17 (3): marked confidential at my request, then I died (my legal representative asks): barred; if I am still alive and competent: not barred.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S17 BARS`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `FACTUAL` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ACCESS YES`
-- Order: an old opinion also barred by law gets the s 10 (1) (d) answer.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- may I see this part of my health record` `HSP RECORD` `OPINION` `1 Jan 1990` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OLD OPINION`
#ASSERT `s 17 -- the part is subject to confidentiality` `BY SOMEONE ELSE` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17 -- the part is subject to confidentiality` `NOT CONFIDENTIAL` TRUE FALSE)

§ `Fees and how access is given (ss 10 (7), 13C)`

#ASSERT `s 10 (7) -- do I have to pay for access` `INSPECT` EQUALS `no fee: the right to inspect is not subject to a fee (s 10 (7))`
#ASSERT `s 10 (7) -- do I have to pay for access` `COPY` EQUALS `a fee may be charged, if the Minister has determined one under s 34, and access can be withheld until it is paid (s 10 (7), s 13 (2) (d) (ii))`
#ASSERT `s 10 (7) -- do I have to pay for access` `EXPLAIN` EQUALS `a fee may be charged, if the Minister has determined one under s 34, and access can be withheld until it is paid (s 10 (7), s 13 (2) (d) (ii))`
#ASSERT `s 13C -- how must I be given access` `INSPECT` EQUALS `the record (or a print-out) is made available to you at a time, and a place in the ACT, stated in a written notice (s 13C (2) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 13C -- how must I be given access` `COPY` EQUALS `you get a copy; or an accurate summary if you agree; or, for a part made before 1 February 1998 that is not copied, a written summary of its factual matters (s 13C (2) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 13C -- how must I be given access` `EXPLAIN` EQUALS `you get a written notice naming when and where in the ACT the record keeper will explain the record, or naming a suitably qualified provider in the ACT who will explain it by arrangement with you (s 13C (2) (c))`

§ `Asking for access (s 12)`

#ASSERT `s 12 (2) (d) -- must my request be in writing` `ME ASKING` FALSE EQUALS `ORAL OK`
#ASSERT `s 12 (2) (d) -- must my request be in writing` `PARENT ASKING` FALSE EQUALS `WRITING NEEDED`
#ASSERT `s 12 (2) (d) -- must my request be in writing` `PARENT ASKING` TRUE EQUALS `ORAL OK`
#ASSERT `s 12 (2) (d) -- must my request be in writing` `GUARDIAN ASKING` FALSE EQUALS `WRITING NEEDED`
#ASSERT `s 12 (2) (d) -- must my request be in writing` `REP ASKING` FALSE EQUALS `WRITING NEEDED`
-- Finding 2: an immediate family member of a deceased consumer is not in s 12 (2) (d).
#ASSERT `s 12 (2) (d) -- must my request be in writing` `FAMILY ASKING` FALSE EQUALS `ORAL OK`

#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ME ASKING` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REQUEST OK`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `ME ASKING` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REQUEST INCOMPLETE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `ME ASKING` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REQUEST INCOMPLETE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `ME ASKING` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REQUEST INCOMPLETE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ME ASKING` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REQUEST OK`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ME ASKING` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ORAL PUT IN WRITING`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `GUARDIAN ASKING` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REQUEST INCOMPLETE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `PARENT ASKING` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REQUEST OK`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is my request properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `PARENT ASKING` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REQUEST INCOMPLETE`

§ `The answer and the access: days (ss 9, 13, 13B)`

-- Received 2 March 2026: answer by 16 March (2 weeks); access by 1 April (30 days).
#ASSERT `s 13 -- by when must my request be answered` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` EQUALS `16 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT `s 13 -- by when must my request be answered` `2 Mar 2026` TRUE `30 Mar 2026` EQUALS `30 Mar 2026`
-- An agreed day earlier than the Act's is not a "longer period" (s 9).
#ASSERT `s 13 -- by when must my request be answered` `2 Mar 2026` TRUE `10 Mar 2026` EQUALS `16 Mar 2026`

#ASSERT `ss 13B, 13BA -- by when must I be given access` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` EQUALS `due by` `1 Apr 2026`
-- Fee paid 20 March: 27 March is earlier than 1 April, so 1 April.
#ASSERT `ss 13B, 13BA -- by when must I be given access` `2 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE `20 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` EQUALS `due by` `1 Apr 2026`
-- Fee paid 25 March: 1 week after is 1 April, the same day.
#ASSERT `ss 13B, 13BA -- by when must I be given access` `2 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE `25 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` EQUALS `due by` `1 Apr 2026`
-- Fee paid 28 March: 4 April is later than 1 April.
#ASSERT `ss 13B, 13BA -- by when must I be given access` `2 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE `28 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` EQUALS `due by` `4 Apr 2026`
#ASSERT `ss 13B, 13BA -- by when must I be given access` `2 Mar 2026` TRUE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` EQUALS `NO FEE DAY`
#ASSERT `ss 13B, 13BA -- by when must I be given access` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` TRUE `15 Apr 2026` EQUALS `due by` `15 Apr 2026`

§ `Is access taken to have been refused (s 13D)`

-- Arguments: received, answer, answered on, fee notice, fee paid, paid on, access given, access given on, evidence not given,
-- arrangements unreasonable, agreed longer, agreed answer day, agreed access day, today.
-- No answer: on the last day (16 March) still in time; the day after, taken to be refused.
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `NO ANSWER` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `16 Mar 2026` EQUALS `NOT YET`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `NO ANSWER` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `17 Mar 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN REFUSED NO ANSWER`
-- Access given on the 14th day (16 March): in time.
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `16 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` TRUE `16 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `20 Mar 2026` EQUALS `NOT REFUSED IN TIME`
-- Access given on the 15th day (17 March): the answer was late, so taken to be refused under s 13.
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `17 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` TRUE `17 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `20 Mar 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN REFUSED NO ANSWER`
-- Fee notice on 10 March, never paid: no access day runs.
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `10 Mar 2026` TRUE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `20 Apr 2026` EQUALS `NOT YET FEE`
-- Fee paid 28 March: access day 4 April; on 4 April still in time, on 5 April taken to be refused; given on 4 April, in time.
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `10 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE `28 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `4 Apr 2026` EQUALS `NOT YET`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `10 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE `28 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `5 Apr 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN REFUSED LATE ACCESS`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `10 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE `28 Mar 2026` TRUE `4 Apr 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `9 Apr 2026` EQUALS `NOT REFUSED IN TIME`
-- No fee: a notice that access will be given, but none given; 1 April still in time, 2 April taken to be refused.
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `NOT YET`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Apr 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN REFUSED LATE ACCESS`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `ACCESS ANSWER` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` TRUE `2 Apr 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `9 Apr 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN REFUSED LATE ACCESS`
-- A refusal notice in time is a refusal, not a deemed one; a refusal notice after 2 weeks is taken first as no answer in time.
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `REFUSAL NOTICE` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `20 Mar 2026` EQUALS `REFUSED BY NOTICE`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `REFUSAL NOTICE` `20 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `20 Mar 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN REFUSED NO ANSWER`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `REFERRAL NOTICE` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `20 Apr 2026` EQUALS `NOT REFUSED REFERRED`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- is access taken to have been refused` `2 Mar 2026` `NO ANSWER` `2 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `20 Apr 2026` EQUALS `NOT REFUSED EVIDENCE`
